# Vercel only needs console/ (built per vercel.json's buildCommand) and api/
# (the serverless function, with its own minimal api/requirements.txt -- see
# api/index.py's module docstring). Everything else is the full local/dev
# project: real ML dependencies (numpy/scikit-learn/shap/river -- river pulls
# in llvmlite, which fails to build in Vercel's Python build sandbox), the
# real network-namespace testbed, tests, docs, research writeups. None of it
# belongs in the deployed function, and letting Vercel's framework
# auto-detection see the root pyproject.toml makes it try to build the whole
# thing as one FastAPI app instead of respecting vercel.json's own build/
# rewrite config -- this is what actually broke the first git-linked deploy
# (see decisions.md's dated entry).
# NOT argus/ wholesale: api/index.py genuinely imports argus.evidence.bundle,
# argus.evidence.replay, and argus.respond.{guard,ladder} at runtime -- pure
# standard-library code with no ML dependency (see api/index.py's own module
# docstring). Excluding those broke the first fixed deploy
# (ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'argus'). Exclude only the
# subpackages/files api/index.py's import graph never reaches.
argus/api/
argus/behavior/
argus/collector/
argus/correlate/
argus/data/
argus/db/
argus/detect/
argus/features/
argus/registry/
argus/respond/adapters/
argus/risk/
argus/sim/
argus/testbed/
argus/verify/
argus/pipeline.py
argus/schemas.py
compose/
data/
docs/
eval/
research/
resume/
results/
scripts/
tests/
pyproject.toml
uv.lock
